  "outcome": "Direction is right: network prediction rises at every one of the 20 steps, from 137 HV at x=0 to 525 HV at x=2, steepest from x=0.3 to about x=0.8 and flattening above x=1.2. Against as-cast measurements in the file it is too high at x=0.6 (predicted 343, one test-side measurement 228) and too low at x=0.9 (predicted 442, one test-side measurement 511): the network draws a smooth ramp where the measurements show a sharper jump. Not an independent physics test: Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloys are among the training rows (as cast at x=0.3, 1.0, 1.5, 2.5, 3.0; annealed at x=0.25 to 1.5), so part of this is recall. The trees give the same overall rise but in steps and not monotonically."
